	<string id="st_body_hint_head_fine">
		<text>Head's fine.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="st_body_hint_head_sore">
		<text>Head's buzzing, but I can think.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="st_body_hint_head_bad">
		<text>Temples pounding, vision swimming. A couple more like that and I'm done.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="st_body_hint_head_wrecked">
		<text>The next hit to the head will finish me. A medkit, now.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="st_body_hint_head_concussion">
		<text>Stunned. Ears ringing, can barely hear a thing.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="st_body_hint_body_fine">
		<text>Chest and gut are fine.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="st_body_hint_body_sore">
		<text>Ribs ache, breathing hurts a bit.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="st_body_hint_body_bad">
		<text>Every breath hurts. Won't last long like this.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="st_body_hint_body_wrecked">
		<text>Insides are a mess. One more hit and that's it.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="st_body_hint_arm_fine">
		<text>Arm's fine.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="st_body_hint_arm_sore">
		<text>Arm's sore, but it holds.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="st_body_hint_arm_bad">
		<text>The arm doesn't listen well.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="st_body_hint_arm_wrecked">
		<text>The arm barely holds anything.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="st_body_hint_arm_light">
		<text>Arm aches, the barrel drifts. A medkit or some rest will do.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="st_body_hint_arm_severe">
		<text>Feels like the bone. Reloading like a rookie, the barrel wanders. I need a splint.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="st_body_hint_leg_fine">
		<text>Leg's fine.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="st_body_hint_leg_sore">
		<text>Leg's sore, but I walk fine.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="st_body_hint_leg_bad">
		<text>Hard to put weight on the leg. Slow, and I tire fast.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="st_body_hint_leg_wrecked">
		<text>The leg barely holds me. Won't get far like this.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="st_body_hint_leg_light">
		<text>Leg aches, I'm limping. Rest or a medkit.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="st_body_hint_leg_severe">
		<text>Feels broken. No running, I need a splint.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="st_body_hint_extra_bleeding">
		<text>Bleeding. Should bandage it.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="st_body_hint_extra_green">
		<text>The artifact holds it together, but it's not healed yet. A medkit would set it.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="st_body_hint_explainer">
		<text>Wounds don't just go away. A light one heals in half an hour once I'm patched up. A bad one needs a splint, a good medkit or a long sleep.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="st_body_hint_name_temp">
		<text>Temporary health</text>
	</string>
	<string id="st_body_hint_name_pain">
		<text>Pain</text>
	</string>
	<string id="st_body_hint_explainer_light">
		<text>A light injury heals by itself: half an hour once the limb is patched up to at least three quarters. A plain medkit clears it at once.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="st_body_hint_explainer_fracture">
		<text>A fracture is set with a splint, a survival kit or an army medkit: you can run in a splint, and it knits in a day (twice as fast asleep). A scientific medkit sets two at once.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="st_body_hint_explainer_temp">
		<text>An artifact or a bandage patches me up in a hurry (green): it holds, but heals slowly. A medkit or sleep makes it last.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="st_body_hint_explainer_pain">
		<text>Pain builds up from wounds and fractures. Left alone, it can knock me out. Morphine or vodka help.</text>
	</string>
